<title>SINGAPORE: Singapore Power, Enron to invest in China power.</title>
<headline>Singapore Power, Enron to invest in China power.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-06-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Singapore Power said on Friday its subsidiary, Singapore Power International (SPI), had formed a partnership with Enron International to invest in China's electricity market.</p>
<p>&quot;The new company, EnSing Power Pte Ltd, with 50-50 equity share, will focus on generation projects of 50 megawatts or lower throughout China,&quot; the state electricity and gas utility said in a statement.</p>
<p>&quot;The company will develop new projects as well as acquire existing plants,&quot; it said.</p>
<p>-- Singapore newsroom (65-870-3571)</p>
